{
  "_comment": [
    "M7.1 fixture: the virtual-heavy host.",
    "",
    "Two physical Ethernet ports buried under Docker bridges, a Tailscale",
    "tunnel, WireGuard and a pile of container veth endpoints.",
    "",
    "The Docker bridge and tailscale0 carry routable addresses and the tunnel",
    "carries a default route, which is exactly the combination that makes a",
    "naive analyser offer 'docker0' as the uplink. Everything that would fool a",
    "name-based or address-based rule is present here on purpose.",
    "",
    "Note the two default routes: the physical uplink and the tunnel. A host",
    "with more than one default route is an ordinary host, so the analysis must",
    "record the fact without calling it broken."
  ],
